251
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,110
Remember you and Tony De Marco?

252
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:32,320
- Oh, yeah.     - Well, it's like that. With feelings.

253
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,260
Oh, wow, are you in trouble!

254
00:16:35,530 --> 00:16:39,330
Okay, okay. I am just going to get up, go to work...

255
00:16:39,490 --> 00:16:42,200
...and not think about him all day.

256
00:16:42,370 --> 00:16:45,330
Or else I'm just gonna get up and go to work.

257
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,130
- Oh, wish me luck!     - What for?

258
00:16:47,330 --> 00:16:50,630
I'm gonna go get one of those job things.

259
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,220
- Hey, Monica.     - Hey, Franny. Welcome back.

260
00:17:01,390 --> 00:17:02,890
How was Florida?

261
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:04,790
You had sex, didn't you?

262
00:17:06,270 --> 00:17:07,310
How do you do that?

263
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:12,230
- So, who?     - You know Paul?

264
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:14,360
Paul, the wine guy?

265
00:17:14,530 --> 00:17:16,110
Oh, yeah, I know Paul.

266
00:17:18,660 --> 00:17:21,160
You mean, you know Paul like I know Paul?

267
00:17:21,370 --> 00:17:23,660
Are you kidding? I take credit for Paul.

268
00:17:23,830 --> 00:17:27,960
Before me, there was no snap in his turtle for two years.

269
00:17:31,210 --> 00:17:33,760
Of course it was a line.

270
00:17:34,170 --> 00:17:36,840
Why? Why would anybody do something like that?

271
00:17:37,050 --> 00:17:40,300
We're looking for an answer more sophisticated than:

272
00:17:40,470 --> 00:17:42,390
"To get you into bed."

273
00:17:43,350 --> 00:17:45,020
Is it me?

274
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:48,730
Is it like I have some sort of beacon that only dogs...

275
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:51,520
...and men with severe emotional problems can hear?

276
00:17:51,730 --> 00:17:54,150
All right, come here. Give me your feet.

277
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,990
I just thought he was nice, you know?

278
00:18:05,870 --> 00:18:08,730
I can't believe you didn't know it was a line.

279
00:18:13,210 --> 00:18:14,250
Guess what.

280
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:16,210
- You got a job?     - Are you kidding?

281
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:18,050
I'm trained for nothing.

282
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:21,930
I was laughed out of 12 interviews today.

283
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:23,640
Yet you're surprisingly upbeat.

284
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:27,350
Well, you would be too if you found Joan and David boots on sale...

285
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:29,270
...50 percent off.

286
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:31,270
Oh, how well you know me.

287
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:35,360
They're my new "I don't need a job or my parents.

288
00:18:35,610 --> 00:18:37,780
I've got great boots" boots.

289
00:18:39,150 --> 00:18:41,360
- How'd you pay for them?     - Uh, credit card.

290
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:43,570
And who pays for that?

291
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:46,330
Um, my father.

292
00:18:48,910 --> 00:18:51,080
You can't live off your parents your whole life.

293
00:18:51,290 --> 00:18:54,960
I know that. That's why I was getting married.

294
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:58,340
Give her a break. It's hard being on your own for the first time.

295
00:18:58,510 --> 00:19:00,010
- Thank you.     - You're welcome.

296
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:02,890
I remember when I first came to this city, I was 14.

297
00:19:03,050 --> 00:19:05,930
My mom had killed herself and my stepdad was back in prison.

298
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:08,140
And I got here, and I didn't know anybody.

299
00:19:08,310 --> 00:19:11,690
I ended up living with this albino guy who was cleaning windshields...

300
00:19:11,850 --> 00:19:15,650
...outside Port Authority. And then he killed himself.

301
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:20,740
And then I found aromatherapy. So believe me, I know exactly how you feel.

302
00:19:24,370 --> 00:19:27,120
The word you're looking for is:

303
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:28,950
"Anyway..."

304
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:34,250
All right. You ready?

305
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:36,130
- I don't think so.     - Oh, come on.

306
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:37,880
Cut. Cut.

307
00:19:38,090 --> 00:19:41,050
Cut, cut, cut.

308
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:45,600
- Hey.     - All right.

309
00:19:45,850 --> 00:19:47,560
Welcome to the real world.

310
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:50,520
It sucks. You're gonna love it.

311
00:19:57,440 --> 00:20:00,780
Well, that's it. You gonna crash on the couch?

312
00:20:00,990 --> 00:20:04,320
- No. No, I gotta go home sometime.     - Are you gonna be okay?

313
00:20:04,490 --> 00:20:05,990
Yeah.

314
00:20:07,030 --> 00:20:09,310
Look what I just found on the floor.

315
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:12,460
What?

316
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,420
That's Paul's watch.

317
00:20:14,580 --> 00:20:16,670
You can just put it back where you found it.

318
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:21,760
Oh, boy. All right. Good night, everybody.

319
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:22,970
Good night.

320
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:35,520
- Oh, sorry.     - No. Oh, no. Go.

321
00:20:35,690 --> 00:20:37,650
- No, have it, really.     - Split it?

322
00:20:37,810 --> 00:20:39,820
- Okay.     - Okay.

323
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:42,780
Thanks.

324
00:20:43,490 --> 00:20:47,070
You probably didn't know this, but back in high school I had...

325
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:49,480
...a major crush on you.

326
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:51,700
I knew.

327
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:54,330
You did? Oh.

328
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:58,730
I figured you thought I was Monica's geeky older brother.

329
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:00,880
I did.

330
00:21:05,510 --> 00:21:07,340
Listen, do you think...

331
00:21:07,510 --> 00:21:11,610
And try not to let my vulnerability become any kind of a factor here.

332
00:21:13,100 --> 00:21:16,980
Do you think it would be okay if I ask you out sometime, maybe?

333
00:21:18,230 --> 00:21:20,060
Yeah.

334
00:21:20,520 --> 00:21:21,820
Maybe.

335
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:24,650
Okay.

336
00:21:29,410 --> 00:21:31,870
Okay, maybe I will.

337
00:21:35,830 --> 00:21:37,960
- Good night.     - Good night.

338
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:53,220
See you.

339
00:21:54,930 --> 00:21:57,350
Wait, wait. Hey, what's with you?

340
00:21:59,650 --> 00:22:02,320
I just grabbed a spoon.

341
00:22:10,490 --> 00:22:11,950
Can't believe what I'm hearing.

342
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:13,870
I can't believe What I'm hearing here

343
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:16,250
- What? I said you had...     - What? I said you had...

344
00:22:17,290 --> 00:22:19,750
- Would you stop?     - Oh, was I doing it again?

345
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,790
Yes.

346
00:22:22,840 --> 00:22:24,840
Would anybody like more coffee?

347
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:29,180
Did you make it or are you just serving it?

348
00:22:29,340 --> 00:22:32,640
- I'm just serving it.     - I'll have a cup of coffee.

349
00:22:33,100 --> 00:22:34,350
Kids, new dream.

350
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:38,430
I'm in Las Vegas. I'm Liza Minnelli.

